# #175 (owner's log, build 4c241d1df3, a TV episode, 2026-11-06):
# storage powered off while a video played; the index window's next read
# met the power-up (600-700 ms on flash, 2-4 s on a disk) in the video
# thread: "thread late", then "dropped GOPs" and 5-10 s of concealment.
# Here the episode plays twice against storage that powers off after a
# short hold (stor_tune), with the device's wake on flash (700 ms) and a
# disk's worst (3000 ms), and an index window of 480 records (20 s at
# 24 fps, video_fault window) so it is read ahead several times a play:
#  p0-p1  the 700 ms wake: storage powers up during the play, on the
#         buffering thread (the reader), never on the video thread; the
#         thread is never late by a wake (700 ms or more);
#  q0-q1  the same with a 3000 ms wake (2400 ms or more);
#  both   the play's end line: the index was read ahead at least once and
#         never in the video thread ("here" 0).
# Why not "no thread late, no dropped GOPs" at all: the simulator's audio
# clock jumps back about 1.5 s every 3 s (a seek each time), and with
# storage never powered off the same play logs lates up to 484 ms and
# GOPs dropped after those seeks (control run, 2026-11-06).  The old code
# fails every line below: "sim stor on by=video", 731-744 ms and
# 2979-3014 ms late, "here" 3 and more.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui-video scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p19-video-wake.script
#   python3 scripts/check_trace.py out/shots/ipodui-p19-video-wake/sim.log tests/ui/ipodui-p19-video-wake.script
# needs: video
# needs: soak
# golden: skip
# timeout: 300
# logbetween: p0 p1 sim stor on by=buffering
# logbetween: p0 p1 no sim stor on by=video
# logbetween: p0 p1 no video: thread late \(ms past its wait, audio ms\) \(([7-9]\d\d|\d{4,}),
# logbetween: p1 q0 video: end: index reads ahead, here \([1-9]\d*, 0\)
# logbetween: q0 q1 sim stor on by=buffering
# logbetween: q0 q1 no sim stor on by=video
# logbetween: q0 q1 no video: thread late \(ms past its wait, audio ms\) \((2[4-9]\d\d|[3-9]\d{3}|\d{5,}),
# logbetween: q1 x0 video: end: index reads ahead, here \([1-9]\d*, 0\)
# nolog: video: index read ahead
# nolog: video: stopped, BCM given back
# nolog: video: image lost
# nolog: CPU FALLBACK
wait 4000
mkdir /.rockbox/soak    # hidden: never in the library
copy ../../build/soak-fixtures/soak.m4v /.rockbox/soak/wake.m4v
stor_tune 1500 500      # off 1.5 s after the last access
stor_pwrup 700          # the owner's flash adapter (600-700 ms)
video_fault window 480
video_screen /.rockbox/soak/wake.m4v
wait 4000
expect_video 20 playing
ab_mark p0
wait 60000
expect_video 600 playing
ab_mark p1
key MENU                # stop
wait 2000
stor_pwrup 3000         # a disk's worst wake
video_screen /.rockbox/soak/wake.m4v
wait 6000
expect_video 20 playing
ab_mark q0
wait 60000
expect_video 600 playing
ab_mark q1
key MENU
wait 2000
ab_mark x0
shot after              # the list again (shots.sh wants one)
rm_file /.rockbox/soak/wake.m4v   # nothing left for the next script
